{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":285,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"“Behold, my eye has seen all this. My ear has heard and understood it.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":879},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":286,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"What you know, I know also. I am not inferior to you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":882},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":287,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"“Surely I would speak to the Almighty. I desire to reason with God.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":886},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":288,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"But you are forgers of lies. You are all physicians of no value.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":889},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":289,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"Oh that you would be completely silent! Then you would be wise.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":892},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":290,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"Hear now my reasoning. Listen to the pleadings of my lips.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":895},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":291,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"Will you speak unrighteously for God, and talk deceitfully for him?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":898},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":292,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"Will you show partiality to him? Will you contend for God?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":901},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":293,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"Is it good that he should search you out? Or as one deceives a man, will you deceive him?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":904},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":294,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"He will surely reprove you if you secretly show partiality.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":907},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":295,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"Won’t his majesty make you afraid and his dread fall on you?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":910},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":296,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"Your memorable sayings are proverbs of ashes. Your defenses are defenses of clay.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":913},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":297,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"“Be silent! Leave me alone, that I may speak. Let come on me what will.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":917},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":298,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"Why should I take my flesh in my teeth, and put my life in my hand?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":921},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":299,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"Behold, he will kill me. I have no hope. Nevertheless, I will maintain my ways before him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":924},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":300,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"This also will be my salvation, that a godless man will not come before him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":928},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":301,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"Listen carefully to my speech. Let my declaration be in your ears.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":931},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":302,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"See now, I have set my cause in order. I know that I am righteous.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":934},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":303,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"Who is he who will contend with me? For then I would hold my peace and give up the spirit.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":937},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":304,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"“Only don’t do two things to me, then I will not hide myself from your face:","is_omitted":0,"source_line":941},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":305,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"withdraw your hand far from me, and don’t let your terror make me afraid.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":944},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":306,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"Then call, and I will answer, or let me speak, and you answer me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":947},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":307,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"How many are my iniquities and sins? Make me know my disobedience and my sin.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":950},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":308,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"Why do you hide your face, and consider me your enemy?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":953},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":309,"verse_start":25,"verse_end":25,"verse_label":"25","text":"Will you harass a driven leaf? Will you pursue the dry stubble?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":956},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":310,"verse_start":26,"verse_end":26,"verse_label":"26","text":"For you write bitter things against me, and make me inherit the iniquities of my youth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":959},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":311,"verse_start":27,"verse_end":27,"verse_label":"27","text":"You also put my feet in the stocks, and mark all my paths. You set a bound to the soles of my feet,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":962},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":13,"verse_ordinal":312,"verse_start":28,"verse_end":28,"verse_label":"28","text":"though I am decaying like a rotten thing, like a garment that is moth-eaten.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":966}]}